meta {
  name: incidents
  seq: 1
}

docs {
  Incident shape:

  ```json
  {
    "id": "uuid",
    "title": "Core router down",
    "description": "",
    "severity": "critical",
    "status": "open",
    "source": "snmp",
    "reporter_id": "uuid",
    "monitor_id": "uuid",
    "acknowledged_at": null,
    "resolved_at": null,
    "closed_at": null,
    "created_at": "...",
    "updated_at": "..."
  }
  ```

  `severity`: `critical` | `high` | `medium` | `low`

  `monitor_id` is set only on incidents the scheduler opened automatically for a monitor with
  `auto_create_incident` on (source `monitor`, severity `critical`). Filter with `?monitor_id=`.

  `status` transitions: `open` -> `acknowledged` -> `resolved` -> `closed`.
  Any non-closed status may jump straight to `closed`. `resolved` may reopen to `open`.
  Each transition stamps the matching `*_at` timestamp.
}
